  "equipment_type": "Sensor (fixed gas detector)",
  "applies_to": "New Cosmos PS-7-M series extractive pump gas detectors (main unit with base unit) over RS-485 Modbus RTU or Ethernet Modbus TCP, communication specifications guide GAE-159-01.",
  "summary": "The New Cosmos PS-7-M is a pump-type fixed gas detector whose base unit has RS-485 Modbus RTU and Ethernet Modbus TCP ports. All data are 16-bit holding registers: current gas concentration, full-scale code, a packed device status word with alarm and fault flags, alarm settings, test and maintenance mode controls and identity data. This map covers the main published registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The table gives each register as a Modicon number (40001-41321) plus a relative address in hex that goes on the wire: 40001 = relative 0, 41039 = relative 0x40E (1038). The manual's examples read 41039 at relative address 1038."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "PS-7-M Communication Specifications Guide",
    "doc_number": "GAE-159-01",
    "revision_date": "2024-04",
    "url": "https://dodtec.com/amfile/file/download/file/357/product/351/",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "pp. 8-9 printed (RS-485 and TCP specifications), pp. 42-48 printed (register address map, PDF pp. 46-52), p. 55 printed (full-scale code table)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The guide is a New Cosmos document hosted by the US distributor DOD Technologies; New Cosmos does not offer it as a public download.",
    "All registers are single 16-bit words. Strings carry two ASCII characters per register, first character in the high byte.",
    "Gas concentration (41039) is an unsigned magnitude; status bit 15 (bit 7 of status byte 1) gives the sign (manual example: 5 with the sign bit set = -5 %). Its unit comes from register 40011 and its full scale from the F.S. code at 41040.",
    "Device status 40516: status byte 1 is the high byte and status byte 2 the low byte (manual example 0x0302 = AL1 and AL2 active while in maintenance mode 2).",
    "Left out: f-value and calibration gas code (ASCII), linear table X/Y pairs (two 8-bit values per register), 41284 Modbus setting change permit (meaning of the value not given), and the IP address/mask/gateway registers 41291-41299.",
    "RS-485 settings are fixed: 9600 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit. The unit ID (1-254) is set on DIP switches and is also the last octet of the IP address for Modbus TCP."
  ],
